2... Nf6 { The Petrov: Black attacks e4 instead of defending e5, hoping to trade pieces and reach a quiet, equal game. } 3. Nxe5 { Takes the pawn. Black cannot just grab e4 back: after ...Nxe4 the queen move Qe2 sets a trap, so Black first kicks this knight away. } 3... d6 ( 3... Qe7 { Attacks the knight on e5, which has no defender. } 4. d4 { Guards the knight with a pawn. Black gets the e4 pawn back, but the queen will stand in the way of Black's own pieces. } 4... d6 5. Nf3 Qxe4+ 6. Be2 { Blocks the check and gets ready to castle. Then Re1 will hit the queen on the open e-file. } ) ( 3... Bc5 4. d4 { Hits the bishop with gain of time. White is a clean pawn up. } 4... Bb6 5. Nc3 { Develops and guards e4. Plan: Bd3 or Be2, castle, and keep the extra pawn. } ) ( 3... Nxe4 4. Qe2 Qe7 ( 4... d5 5. d3 { Attacks the pinned knight on e4 a second time. It cannot move off the e-file without exposing the king. } 5... Qe7 6. dxe4 Qxe5 7. exd5 { White has won a pawn, and Black's queen is about to be traded or chased. } ) 5. Qxe4 { Wins the knight for nothing: Black's queen cannot guard e4 through White's own knight on e5. ...d6 then hits the knight, so White retreats and stays a pawn up. } 5... d6 6. d4 dxe5 7. dxe5 ) 4. Nf3 { The knight retreats to its best square, central and ready to support d4. Black's d6 pawn was attacking it. } 4... Nxe4 5. d4 { Takes the centre and frees the c1 bishop. White has more space, and Black's knight on e4 has no easy way home. } 5... d5 6. Bd3 { Develops, eyes the knight on e4 and clears the way to castle. Black cannot easily trade it off. } 6... Be7 ( 6... Bd6 7. O-O O-O 8. c4 c6 9. Nc3 Nxc3 10. bxc3 ) 7. O-O { Castles before the centre opens, so the king is safe when lines open. } 7... Nc6 ( 7... Bg4 8. c4 Nc6 9. cxd5 Qxd5 10. Nc3 ) ( 7... O-O 8. c4 Nf6 9. Nc3 Nc6 10. Re1 ) 8. c4 { Hits the d5 pawn, which is what holds Black's knight on e4 in place. White is ahead in development, so opening the centre helps. } 8... Nb4 9. Be2 { Steps back before the knight on b4 can take the bishop. Trading it off would lose time and the bishop pair for nothing. } 9... O-O 10. Nc3 { Develops and attacks the knight on e4, which has to trade itself off. } 10... Bf5 11. a3 { Attacks the knight on b4, so it has to trade itself off. } 11... Nxc3 12. bxc3 { Recaptures towards the centre, so pawns on c3, c4 and d4 give White a strong grip. } 12... Nc6 { Plan: finish development with Re1 and Bf4, and take on d5 with the c-pawn to open lines. If Black leaves the book, castle early and keep the pawns on c4 and d4 to hold the centre. } *
